  The article says the bike taxi driver Lokeswaran was cheated, but the draft's reel_script says "சூளைமேட்டில் பைக்டாக்சி ஓட்டுநரிடம்" and the caption says the crime happened in Choolaimedu; the article does not say where the cheating occurred (only where Deva booked from and where the auto was stopped/where the assault happened), so the location of the crime is not stated in the article.
  The reel_script says Deva said "நண்பர் பணத்துடன் வருவதாகக் கூறி" and the claim that Rs 2,000 would be paid is described as a lure; the article says Deva said a friend was coming with money and the amount would be returned as Rs 2,000 - this matches, but the draft's caption and reel_script describe Deva as having jumped from 'ஓடிக்கொண்டிருந்த ஆட்டோ', which the article does not say (the article says he jumped from an auto passing by, not that it was moving), and the reel_script's "வேறொரு ஆட்டோவில் ஏறித் தப்பினார்" is consistent but the caption's "ஆட்டோவில் இருந்து குதித்து" omits that it was another auto.
  The caption's and reel_script's framing that Lokeswaran was 'விரட்டிச் சென்று' and 'லோகேஸ்வரனும் மோட்டார் சைக்கிளை விட்டுவிட்டு அதே ஆட்டோவில் ஏறினார்' is fine, but the reel_script's line that Deva and his friend 'லோகேஸ்வரனைத் தாக்கி விரட்டினர்' omits that the article says they threatened him with a knife and beat and chased him away - the knife threat is mentioned, so no issue; however the article does not state the victim was 'விரட்டி அடித்தனர்' as a separate attack from the threat, which is acceptable.
  The reel_script's ending sentence 'ஆன்லைன் பயணங்களில் கவனமாக இருங்கள்' in slides_spec is an advisory not from the article, an invented detail, though it is a generic message rather than a factual claim.
  The caption's English line 'Choolaimedu bike taxi cheated, 2 arrested | Chennai news' is a headline-style claim consistent with the article.
